# Buffer

A self-contained, lock-free, single-producer / single-consumer (SPSC) buffer
family for embedded systems (Cortex-M, ESP32, etc.).

- **No locks, no OS dependency** - safe across ISR / task boundaries via
  acquire/release memory ordering (GCC/Clang `__atomic`, plain-read fallback
  for other compilers).
- **No dynamic memory** - all storage is statically allocated by the caller.
- **Cache-line friendly** - hot pointers are 64-byte aligned to avoid false
  sharing on multi-core targets.
- **Small footprint** - two source files and one header, C11.

## Buffer types

| Type                | Element width  | Typical use                                      |
|---------------------|----------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `fifo_spsc`         | fixed (`uintptr_t`) | ISR -> task sample / pointer queue          |
| `fifo_uni_spsc`     | configurable   | byte streams (UART/TCP), frame queues, zero-copy slots |
| `double_buffer_spsc`| fixed (`uintptr_t`) | DMA capture + CPU processing (block swap)   |
| `dual_buffer_spsc`  | configurable   | continuous streams (audio/sensor), independent read/write pacing |

## Quick start

Add `buffer.h`, `circle_fifo_buffer.c` and `double_buffer.c` to your build:

```c
#include "buffer.h"
```

All capacities (item counts) **must be a power of two** - indices are mapped
with `mask = size - 1`.

## Examples

### 1. `fifo_spsc` - queue samples from an ISR to a task

```c
#define CAP 256                        /* power of two */
static fifo_data_type s_buf[CAP];
static struct fifo_spsc s_fifo;

void init(void) { fifo_init(&s_fifo, s_buf, CAP); }

void adc_isr(void)                     /* producer */
{
    fifo_write_data(&s_fifo, adc_value());
}

void app_task(void)                    /* consumer */
{
    fifo_data_type v;
    if (fifo_read_data(&s_fifo, &v))
    {
        handle_sample(v);
    }
}
```

### 2. `fifo_uni_spsc` - UART/TCP byte stream

```c
#define TX_BYTES 512                   /* power of two */
static uint8_t s_tx[TX_BYTES];
static struct fifo_uni_spsc s_fifo;

void init(void) { fifo_uni_init(&s_fifo, s_tx, 1, TX_BYTES); }  /* item_size = 1 */

void uart_send(const uint8_t* data, uint16_t len)   /* producer */
{
    fifo_uni_write_block(&s_fifo, data, len);       /* returns bytes queued */
}

void uart_tx_done_cb(void)             /* consumer, e.g. TX DMA complete */
{
    uint8_t chunk[64];
    uint16_t n = fifo_uni_read_block(&s_fifo, chunk, sizeof(chunk));
    if (n)
    {
        uart_dma_send(chunk, n);
    }
}
```

### 3. `fifo_uni_spsc` - zero-copy frame queue

```c
typedef struct { uint32_t len; uint8_t data[60]; } frame_t;  /* 64 B, DMA-friendly */
#define FRAMES 16                      /* power of two */
static uint8_t s_frames[FRAMES * sizeof(frame_t)];
static struct fifo_uni_spsc s_q;

void init(void) { fifo_uni_init(&s_q, s_frames, sizeof(frame_t), FRAMES); }

void rx(void)                          /* producer: fill the slot in place */
{
    frame_t* f = (frame_t*)fifo_uni_write_acquire(&s_q);
    if (f)
    {
        fill_frame(f);
        fifo_uni_write_commit(&s_q);
    }
}

void app(void)                         /* consumer: peek without copying */
{
    frame_t* f = (frame_t*)fifo_uni_read_peek(&s_q);
    if (f)
    {
        process_frame(f);
        fifo_uni_read_release(&s_q);
    }
}
```

### 4. `double_buffer_spsc` - DMA capture + CPU processing

```c
#define BLOCK 128                      /* power of two */
static double_buffer_data_type s_b1[BLOCK], s_b2[BLOCK];
static struct double_buffer_spsc s_db;

void init(void) { double_buffer_init(&s_db, s_b1, s_b2, BLOCK); }

/* producer: buffers swap automatically when the write side is full and
   the read side is drained */
void dma_done_cb(void)
{
    double_buffer_write_block(&s_db, s_samples, BLOCK);
}

void app_task(void)                    /* consumer */
{
    double_buffer_data_type out[BLOCK];
    uint16_t n = double_buffer_read_block(&s_db, out, BLOCK);
    if (n)
    {
        process(out, n);
    }
}
```

### 5. `dual_buffer_spsc` - continuous audio/sensor stream

```c
typedef int16_t sample_t;
#define N 256                          /* power of two, per buffer */
static uint8_t s_a1[N * sizeof(sample_t)], s_a2[N * sizeof(sample_t)];
static struct dual_buffer_spsc s_db;

void init(void) { dual_buffer_init(&s_db, s_a1, s_a2, sizeof(sample_t), N); }

/* producer: never blocks - spills to the second buffer when the first is full */
uint16_t audio_rx(const sample_t* in, uint16_t n)
{
    return dual_buffer_write_block(&s_db, in, n);
}

/* consumer: reads across both buffers, never blocked by the producer */
void app_task(void)
{
    sample_t chunk[64];
    uint16_t n = dual_buffer_read_block(&s_db, chunk, 64);
    if (n)
    {
        process_audio(chunk, n);
    }
}
```

## API reference

| Buffer | API |
|---|---|
| `fifo_spsc` | `fifo_init`, `fifo_write_data`, `fifo_read_data`, `fifo_write_block`, `fifo_read_block`, `fifo_isfull`, `fifo_isempty`, `fifo_get_count` |
| `fifo_uni_spsc` | `fifo_uni_init`, `fifo_uni_write_block`, `fifo_uni_read_block`, `fifo_uni_write_acquire`, `fifo_uni_write_commit`, `fifo_uni_read_peek`, `fifo_uni_read_release`, `fifo_uni_isfull`, `fifo_uni_isempty`, `fifo_uni_get_count` |
| `double_buffer_spsc` | `double_buffer_init`, `double_buffer_write_data`, `double_buffer_read_data`, `double_buffer_write_block`, `double_buffer_read_block`, `double_buffer_isfull`, `double_buffer_isempty`, `double_buffer_get_count` |
| `dual_buffer_spsc` | `dual_buffer_init`, `dual_buffer_write_block`, `dual_buffer_read_block`, `dual_buffer_isfull`, `dual_buffer_isempty`, `dual_buffer_get_count` |

## Notes

- **SPSC only** - exactly one producer and one consumer; more concurrent
  writers/readers are a data race, synchronize externally.
- **Power of two** - every capacity must be a power of two.
- **Alignment** - for `fifo_uni_spsc` / `dual_buffer_spsc`, use an `item_size`
  multiple of the alignment required by your DMA/CPU (e.g. 4 bytes for DMA);
  hot pointers are 64-byte aligned automatically.
- **No heap** - allocate all storage statically (static arrays or a pool).

